      "name": "ProcessStructureLoop",
      "signature": "void ProcessStructureLoop(int * pData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Iterates through structure elements and processes each item\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load structure count from pData[2] (offset +8)\n2. While count > 0, calculate element pointer: pData[0] + count\n3. Call ProcessStructureLoop callback function with calculated pointer\n4. Continue until count exhausted\n\nParameters:\npData (int *): Pointer to structure with layout:\n  [0] Base address/pointer to element data\n  [2] Element count (32-bit integer at offset +8)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function processes structure and returns when complete",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:35a5d69c6aa19996054f7f44d5ee94a0",
