      "name": "LinkNodeToList",
      "signature": "void LinkNodeToList(int * pNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Link a node into a doubly-linked list structure, updating both forward and backward pointers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load node pointer from pNode[0] into pListNode\n2. If pListNode is null, return (no operation)\n3. Load offset value from pNode[1] into nOffset\n4. Calculate target address:\n   - If nOffset < 0: target = ~nOffset (bitwise NOT)\n   - Otherwise: target = pNode + (nOffset - pListNode[1])\n5. Store pListNode at target address (update backward pointer)\n6. Load updated pNode[0] and pNode[1] values into registers\n7. Write pNode[1] to pListNode[1] (update forward pointer)\n8. Clear pNode[0] to 0\n9. Clear pNode[1] to 0\n\nParameters:\npNode: Pointer to array [2] containing:\n  - pNode[0]: pointer to node to link\n  - pNode[1]: offset value for list position\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pNode[0] is null, function returns without modification\n- Negative offset uses bitwise NOT for direct address computation\n- Positive offset computed relative to pNode and pListNode[1]\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0: Sentinel value for clearing pointers",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:02534d2b6ee2fd8304e486000f75b796",
