      "name": "ExceptionUnwindHandler",
      "signature": "void ExceptionUnwindHandler(PVOID pExceptionFrame, PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "SEH exception unwinding handler. Saves exception handler context, calls RtlUnwind to unwind the stack, clears EH_NESTING flag from exception record, and restores previous handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current ExceptionList pointer (FS:[0]) to local stack variable\n2. Save return address (0x6fb99d75) as unwinding destination\n3. Call RtlUnwind with: pExceptionFrame, pReturnAddress, pExceptionRecord, NULL\n4. After unwinding, clear EH_NESTING flag (0x02) from ExceptionRecord.ExceptionFlags\n5. Restore previous exception handler pointer from saved value\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npExceptionFrame (PVOID) - Stack frame/exception handler context\npExceptionRecord (PEXCEPTION_RECORD) - Exception information record\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Does not return normally; RtlUnwind transfers control\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is SEH personality routine, called by Windows exception handler\n- Unconditionally clears EH_NESTING flag (0xFFFFFFFD mask) from exception flags\n- FS:[0] register access is Windows SEH exception list\n- Return address 0x6fb99d75 is unwinding destination after RtlUnwind\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away (local_8, local_c)",
