      "name": "SearchRangeTable",
      "signature": "int SearchRangeTable(uint dwRangeTable, int nCountdown, int nValue, uint * pnFoundIndex, uint * pnPrevIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Search a range table for an entry containing the given value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load table metadata: pRangeTable+0xC (entry count), pRangeTable+0x10 (array pointer)\n  2. Initialize search: dwCurrentIndex = entry count, dwLastIndex = entry count\n  3. While nCountdown >= 0:\n     a. If dwCurrentIndex == 0xFFFFFFFF, raise error\n     b. Decrement dwCurrentIndex\n     c. Check if nValue in range: array[dwCurrentIndex].lower <= nValue < array[dwCurrentIndex].upper\n     d. If match found (or index=0xFFFFFFFF), update indices and decrement nCountdown\n  4. Increment dwCurrentIndex (undo final decrement)\n  5. Store search results: *pnFoundIndex = dwCurrentIndex, *pnPrevIndex = dwLastIndex\n  6. Validate indices: if dwLastIndex >= entry count OR dwCurrentIndex > dwLastIndex, raise error\n  7. Return pointer to matching entry: array_base + dwCurrentIndex * 0x14\n\nParameters:\n  pRangeTable (uint) - Pointer to range table structure\n  nCountdown (int) - Search countdown/iteration limit\n  nValue (int) - Value to search for in ranges\n  pnFoundIndex (uint *) - Output: index of found range entry\n  pnPrevIndex (uint *) - Output: index of previous entry\n\nReturns:\n  int - Pointer to matching range entry in array (array_base + index * 0x14)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If entry count is 0xFFFFFFFF (error state), raises error\n  - Search validates index bounds at end; out-of-range raises error\n  - 0x14 = 20 bytes per entry (5 DWORDs: range_low, padding, range_high, ?, data_ptr)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xC - Offset to entry count field in table header\n  0x10 - Offset to array pointer field in table header\n  0x14 - Entry size (20 bytes)\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Invalid/error index marker",
