      "sizes": {
        "LoD/1.11": 108,
        "LoD/1.11b": 108,
        "LoD/1.12a": 108,
        "LoD/1.13c": 108,
        "LoD/1.13d": 108
      },
      "name": "UngetcFileBuf",
      "signature": "int UngetcFileBuf(int nChar, FILE * pFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Puts a character back into a file stream buffer for re-reading.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input character is not EOF (0xffffffff)\n2. Check file flags to ensure stream is open and readable/writable\n3. Allocate file buffer if needed via __getbuf\n4. Adjust buffer pointer position (move back one byte)\n5. Write or verify character in buffer at current position\n6. Update file flags to mark unget operation\n7. Return the character (masked to byte) on success, or EOF on failure\n\nParameters:\n  nChar (int): Character to put back, or EOF (0xffffffff) to fail\n  pFile (FILE*): File stream structure with _ptr, _base, _cnt, _flag fields\n\nReturns:\n  (int) Character on success (0-255), or EOF (-1) if operation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns EOF if nChar is already EOF\n  - Returns EOF if file flags indicate write-only or closed stream\n  - Calls __getbuf to allocate buffer if _base is null\n  - Returns EOF if at start of buffer with empty read buffer\n  - If _flag has 0x40 set, verifies character matches what's in buffer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:67c0855c00e7b7a5408f02f9c5ef5adc",
