      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Tail-call wrapper that delegates to DestroyAURGNCollection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the first parameter (pCollection) from the stack at EBP+0xc\n2. Perform a tail jump to DestroyAURGNCollection at 0x6fbf2740\n\nThis wrapper is used as an exception unwinding routine for AURGN collection cleanup.\nThe actual destruction logic (element iteration, deallocation) is implemented in \nDestroyAURGNCollection. This function exists to provide a standardized unwind \ninterface in exception handling or finally-block semantics.\n\nParameters:\n  pCollection [EBP+0xc] - Pointer to AURGN collection to unwrap and destroy\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value (tail calls DestroyAURGNCollection which returns void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - This is a tail-call optimization: control flow transfers directly to \n    DestroyAURGNCollection without a separate return\n  - The function signature appears in function pointer tables used by exception\n    handlers or resource cleanup sequences\n  - Called from DATA reference at 0x6fc3ce50 (likely part of vtable or handler table)\n\nCalling Convention:\n  __stdcall - Callee cleanup after return",
